From 87bf6c2c00d478ded6ef390577ce26dba6797c8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LowBacon <lenni.a.jokitalo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:18:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/25] Masked merge on the card for the title's runs under
 shader writes (VICTORY_GPU_MERGE=1, off by default) (HybridGt)

The title's CPU writes 85,000-102,000 runs a frame of 2-3 bytes each into
pages flights' shaders write (run next12). For a copy in the card's memory
merge_under_writes sent each run up as a copy of its own, 512 a
submission, and past them the submission waited for every flight (77 ms
a frame).

With the switch the runs go to a MergeLog per card copy: (dword, byte
mask) entries for the next send, and the byte runs by (offset, own
number) with the send that took them. At the send (card_before) one
dispatch per copy (CARD_MERGE) writes the masked bytes of the CPU side
into the card side, before that copy's sends, between explicit state
transitions; the merged 64 KiB pieces are hashed again with the sent
ones. The copy-back (card_merge_relay) skips merged runs its fetch did
not see (pending, or sent after it), as it skips sent ranges; runs are
forgotten once a fetch sent after them has been merged.

Tests: merge_log_tests (masks, joined dwords, unseen runs, pruning,
runs merged again); card_merge_tests on the card (every byte checked).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
